00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:10,200
Based on the results, we will provide
a personalized learning path.

237
00:15:11,850 --> 00:15:15,315
We will also organize Vocabulary,
Grammar, Phonics, Reading,

238
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:18,260
and Writing into a structured
literacy curriculum.

239
00:15:18,710 --> 00:15:21,846
This will help students develop
skills in understanding,

240
00:15:21,902 --> 00:15:25,150
making inferences, making
decisions, and expressing ideas.

241
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:28,720
In addition, we plan to
improve our learning reports.

242
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:31,891
We want parents and students
to easily understand

243
00:15:31,946 --> 00:15:35,000
and use information about
learning progress and growth.

244
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:40,326
To summarize, our final direction
is to develop a new program that

245
00:15:40,381 --> 00:15:44,280
builds literacy through detailed
assessment and personalized learning.

246
00:15:44,730 --> 00:15:48,350
We also want to make learning results
and progress clearly visible.

247
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:54,071
To put our product strategy into practice,
we first need to connect national

248
00:15:54,123 --> 00:15:57,780
and state education standards with
our learning system and assessment.

249
00:15:58,230 --> 00:16:01,690
However, education standards
vary across U.S. states.

250
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:08,260
Among the 50 states, 39 have changed CCSS
or use their own curriculum standards.

251
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:14,159
We reviewed ELA standards across
all 50 U.S. states, including

252
00:16:14,228 --> 00:16:17,860
California, New Jersey, New
York, Florida, and Texas.

253
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:22,624
Our plan is to build a common ELA and
Literacy structure while reflecting

254
00:16:22,683 --> 00:16:26,760
each state's standards in assessment
and personalized learning paths.

255
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:29,923
This will help us design
assessments and learning

256
00:16:29,979 --> 00:16:32,360
paths that match local
education standards.

257
00:16:34,110 --> 00:16:36,876
We are also considering
how to turn this product

258
00:16:36,934 --> 00:16:39,470
strategy into an actual
learning experience.

259
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:43,780
Students will select their program,
country, state, and language.

260
00:16:44,230 --> 00:16:48,031
Based on this information, they will
take an online Adaptive Assessment

261
00:16:48,084 --> 00:16:51,510
that reflects local education
standards and learning conditions.

262
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:56,830
We will then use the assessment results
to provide personalized learning.

263
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:00,731
Students will be able to choose
POD workbooks, online learning,

264
00:17:00,786 --> 00:17:03,580
or a combination of both,
depending on their needs.

265
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:06,251
In the long term, we aim to expand this

266
00:17:06,308 --> 00:17:08,870
into a global personalized
learning platform.

267
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:14,130
We plan to provide personalized
learning through three main steps.

268
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:16,838
First, we will set
learning standards based

269
00:17:16,890 --> 00:17:19,200
on each student's country,
state, and grade.

270
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:22,483
Second, we will use Adaptive
Assessment to identify

271
00:17:22,539 --> 00:17:25,150
the student's current
level and learning needs.

272
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:28,157
Third, we will design a
personalized learning

273
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:30,770
path and adjust it based
on learning results.

274
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,427
This will lead to Adaptive
Learning, where each student's

275
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:38,170
next learning steps change
based on their progress.

276
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:40,580
Thank you.

